  "live_records": {
    "q-111349": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111349",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Given that  $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\\}$, find a basis for $\\text{Null}(A).$",
      "worked_solution": "Any vector in $\\text{Null}(A)$ has the form\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nExpanding, we get \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ \\,\\,1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, a basis for $\\text{Null}(A)$ is\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ \\,\\,1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\}\n$$\n\nsince it is a linearly independent set that generates $\\text{Null}(A).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
